# VictoriaMetrics discover

## Gate

Use when the user asks which metrics/labels exist, series shape, TSDB
cardinality, alert/rule inventory, top/active queries, or needs names before
a query. Skip bare "VictoriaMetrics" / "VM" with no discover/query ask.
Load `victoriametrics-safety` with this rule.

Never invent a metric name, label name, or selector — resolve from MCP this
turn or from a name the user pasted.

## Prefer MCP

When a VictoriaMetrics MCP is ready (`user-mcp_victoriametrics`), use these
tools — do not invent a side CLI or raw HTTP client while MCP works:

| Need | Tool | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| List metric names | `metrics` | optional `match`, `start`/`end`, `limit` |
| Label names | `labels` | optional `match`, time window, `limit` |
| Label values | `label_values` | required `label_name`; optional `match` |
| Series selectors | `series` | optional `match`, time window, `limit` |
| Metric type/help | `metrics_metadata` | `metric`, `search`, `type`, `unit`, `limit` |
| Cardinality / TSDB | `tsdb_status` | `topN`, `focusLabel`, `match`, `date` |
| Query usage stats | `metric_statistics` | unused/hot metrics (`le`, `match_pattern`) |
| Active queries | `active_queries` | currently running queries |
| Top queries | `top_queries` | required `topN`; optional `maxLifetime` |
| Alerts inventory | `alerts` | optional `state`, `group`, `limit`/`offset` |
| Rules inventory | `rules` | alert/record filters; `unhealthy` / `noMatch` |

## Discover-before-query ladder

1. Prefer exact metric the user named.
2. Else `metrics` with a tightening `match` selector when the surface is
   known, or `metrics_metadata` with `search` for a keyword in name/help.
3. Read type/help via `metrics_metadata` — counters need `rate()`-style
   rollups; gauges usually do not.
4. `series` with `match` on the chosen metric to see which labels exist.
5. `label_values` for key labels before writing matchers — confirm
   spelling and case (`label_name` required).
6. For "why is this huge?": `tsdb_status` (optionally `focusLabel`) before
   guessing high-cardinality labels; `metric_statistics` for never-queried
   vs hot names.
7. For load/incident context: `active_queries` / `top_queries` /
   `alerts` / `rules` as inventory (not query execution).
8. If several metrics match, list a short shortlist and ask once; do not
   pick a production metric by guess.

## Time windows and limits

- Discovery tools accept `start` / `end` as RFC3339 or Unix epoch when a
  historical window matters.
- Prefer modest `limit` / `topN` on first pulls; raise only when truncated.
- `tsdb_status` `date` defaults to today; use `1970-01-01` only when the
  user asked for global cardinality (heavy).

## Report shape

- Metric / label names actually returned by MCP (not guessed)
- Short type/help note when metadata was used
- Cardinality / alert / top-query notes when those were the ask
- One recommended next step (query, tighter matchers, or cardinality dig)

## Out of scope

- Instant/range MetricsQL execution → `victoriametrics-query`
- Dashboard / Explore UX on other products — own VictoriaMetrics MCP only
- Dumping full alert payloads with secrets → `victoriametrics-safety`
